  "prompt": "Look at the order lines of the two flagship stores BE-01 and LU-01 (store_code 'BE-01' or 'LU-01') with an order_date from 1 January 2025 to 28 February 2025, both days included. Return four columns, in this order: first_order_date (the earliest order_date), last_order_date (the latest order_date), max_units (the most units on a single line) and max_line_revenue_eur (the highest net_revenue_eur on a single line). Every line counts for the two dates; a line with a missing units or net_revenue_eur value is left out of that maximum only. Use exactly these column names. Do not round. The result is a single row. Any row order is fine.",
